Change settings in config.toml, keeping its comments and layout. The file is created if
it doesn't exist.

Keys are dotted, such as `extract.overwrite`, `shell.items.test` or `levels.zstd` (any
codec or method); `beezip settings get` lists them. Nothing is written unless the whole
file still reads: an unknown key or a value of the wrong type fails with `InvalidArgs`.
The app's later jobs use the new settings at once; other BeeZip processes read them when
they start.

Usage: beezip settings set [OPTIONS] [KEY=VALUE]...

Arguments:
  [KEY=VALUE]...
          Settings to change: VALUE is TOML (19, false, ['C:/a']), or a bare word for a string

Options:
      --reset <KEY>
          Put a setting back to its default; repeatable

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Global options:
      --output <FORMAT>
          How to print results; ndjson streams every job event

          Possible values:
          - human:  Text for people
          - json:   One JSON document on stdout: the output, or `{"error": {...}}`
          - ndjson: Every job event as a JSON line on stdout, ending with `Finished`, `Failed` or
            `Cancelled`
          
          [default: human]

  -q, --quiet
          No progress bars or info messages; warnings still print
